By definition of $\Delta_\eta(f)$ we know that \[\eta
orm{f}_1\abs{\Delta}\le \sum_{\gamma\in\Delta} \lvert \widehat{f}(\gamma)vert.\] There exists some $c_\gamma\in bc$ with $\lvert c_\gammavert=1$ for all $\gamma$ such that \[\lvert \widehat{f}(\gamma)vert=c_\gamma\widehat{f}(\gamma)=c_\gamma \sum_{x\in G}f(x)\overline{\gamma(x)}.\] Interchanging the sums, therefore, \[\eta
orm{f}_1\abs{\Delta}\le \sum_{x\in G}f(x)\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta} c_\gamma \overline{\gamma(x)}.\] By H"{o}lder's inequality the right-hand side is at most \[ rac{\sum_x \abs{f(x)}}^{1-1/m} rac{\sum_x \abs{f(x)}\abs{\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta}c_\gamma\overline{\gamma(x)}}^m}^{1/m}.\] Taking $m$th powers, therefore, we have \[\eta^m\abs{\Delta}^m
orm{f}_1\le \sum_{x}\abs{f(x)}\abs{\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta}c_\gamma\overline{\gamma(x)}}^m.\] By assumption we can bound $\abs{f(x)}\le \abs{f(x)}
u(x)^{1/2}$, and therefore by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality the right-hand side is bounded above by \[
orm{f}_2 rac{\sum_x 
u(x)\abs{\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta}c_\gamma\overline{\gamma(x)}}^{2m}}^{1/2}.\] Squaring and simplifying, we deduce that \[\eta^{2m}\abs{\Delta}^{2m} rac{
orm{f}_1^2}{
orm{f}_2^2}\le \sum_x 
u(x)\abs{\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta}c_\gamma\overline{\gamma(x)}}^{2m}.\] Expanding out the power, the right-hand side is equal to \[\sum_x 
